          "cont": [],
          "key": "description",
          "lead": [],
          "value": "\"bsc memory — the session-memory surface (#memory): capture the findings, decisions, lessons and parked threads a session generates but has no plan item for, so they don't evaporate when the terminal closes. A thin, tagged, TYPED-EDGE log over the shared bsc-json-store (memory.db). Entries carry a horizon (now vs future) and typed links — {ref, rel} to another memory, a graph record id, a symbol anchor, or a plan ref — so memory is a graph you traverse, told apart from a flat pile of notes.\""
        }
